# Local-only chinese startup runbook: contains a developer's absolute path and
# test-account plaintext password. Never share.
/启动说明.md

# Local-only deploy/start/stop helpers with this machine's absolute paths
# (repo root, system python, nginx). Deployment-specific. No PHP any more.
/start-all.ps1
/stop-all.ps1
/deploy.ps1

# Local POC demo artifacts (plan HTML, demo scripts, screenshots, recordings).
# Never commit these to the remote repository.
/doc/
ref/
**/.dev.vars
.cursor/
local/
node_modules/

# cow cli
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.cow.pid

# Desktop backend packaging: keep the source files (spec/requirements/script)
# tracked even though the generic build/ rule above ignores them, but never
# track the build outputs or local venv.
!desktop/build/
desktop/build/*
!desktop/build/cowagent-backend.spec
!desktop/build/requirements-desktop.txt
!desktop/build/build-backend.sh
# The packaging guard the release workflows run before PyInstaller. Allow-listed
# for the same reason as the script above, and it matters more than most: a guard
# that never reaches the runner is a guard that never ran, and the workflows would
# fail on a missing file rather than on the dependency it exists to catch.
!desktop/build/check-skill-dependencies.py
# The other two build steps the workflows and build-backend.sh call. Same reason
# as above — and these two guard the class of failure that builds cleanly and
# ships broken: `check-python-syntax.py` (the bundle ships Python 3.11 while a
# developer's venv is newer) and `verify-backend-bundle.py` (starts the frozen
# executable the way an installed app does and runs a real tool through it).
!desktop/build/check-python-syntax.py
!desktop/build/verify-backend-bundle.py
!desktop/build/build-feishu-vendor.py
!desktop/build/entitlements.mac.plist
!desktop/build/installer.nsh

# Icon authoring scratch dir: intermediate assets used to produce the final
# icons. Only the finished icons under desktop/resources/ should be committed.
desktop/resources/.icon-work/

# Bundled ripgrep binary: downloaded by CI (release workflow) at build time,
# never committed — it's a multi-MB platform-specific executable.
desktop/resources/bin/

.wrangler/

# Obsidian editor workspace (accidental commit vector; never part of the app)
.obsidian/

# FORK-ONLY IGNORE RULES (RongAI fork of CowAgent) — keep this section LAST.
#
# Everything below this banner is this fork's local convention, not upstream's.
# Keeping it in its own labelled section means an upstream merge that adds
# ignore rules above can never silently overwrite (or be overwritten by) this
# one: on conflict, keep both sections with this one intact (task 9.6).
#
# This section is kept even when it is empty, because its value is the stable
# boundary rather than any particular rule. It most recently held `/openspec/`,
# which was removed when the OpenSpec specs, changes and archive were moved into
# version control: they are the authoritative requirement baseline (see
# .cursor/rules/openspec-spec-authority.mdc), so leaving them out meant a fresh
# clone could not read its own specs and `scripts/check_change_deltas.py` had
# nothing to check.
# =============================================================================

# The bare `config.yaml` rule above is upstream's, for its runtime config at the
# repo root; being unanchored it also matches at depth and would silently drop
# OpenSpec's own config -- which is *source*, because it carries this fork's spec
# rules and context. Re-include it explicitly.
!openspec/config.yaml


# The local marketing demo is its own repository (`marketing-demo/.git`) holding
# nothing but build output. Committing it here would record a gitlink with no
# remote to fetch, so a fresh clone could not materialise it; it stays local.
/marketing-demo/

# Codex CLI's scratch tree for that same deck (node_modules, the .pptx and its
# rendered slide PNGs). Machine-local build output, never source.
/.codex-build/

# Created as a side effect of tests/test_skill_dependencies_lock.py, which passes
# a repo-root-relative path ("does-not-exist") to exercise the missing-directory
# branch; the code under test then writes skills_config.json into it. A stray
# test artifact, not source, and it must not be committed.
/does-not-exist/
# FuXi session state (settings, scheduled-task locks, scratchpad symlinks)
.fuxi/

# Persistent Agent Mail credentials and npm runtime created by the optional compose overlay.
docker/agent-mail-data/
# Local runtime data written into the workspace on source deployments
# (config.py: get_data_root() falls back to the workspace root). These are
# private per-instance artifacts, not source, so keep them out of git.
/identity.db
# Timestamped pre-migration dumps of the same database (`identity.db.bak-<stamp>`,
# `identity.db.prt<n>-...`), written next to it by migration/acceptance scripts.
/identity.db.bak-*
/identity.db.prt*
/memory/
# Instance-level Web branding state (name/logo/snapshots/rollback) written by
# channel/web/branding.py under get_data_root(); see /identity.db above.
/branding/

# Scratch debug instance (`--data-root dbg` local runs): carries its own
# identity.db (real user rows and password hashes) and agent workspace. Runtime
# state for reproducing a bug, never source; see /identity.db above.
/dbg/

# Transient verification scratch files (launcher scripts + their data dir).
# `.tmp_*` is the general rule; the named entries below document the two
# harnesses that were used before it existed (browser walk in evidence.md §10.6).
.tmp_*
.tmp_verify_launcher.py
.tmp_verify_server.py
.tmp_verify_data/

# README files are not synced to the remote repository.
README*.md
# ...but a sub-Agent's guide is a *shipped asset*, not repository
# documentation: the feature hands it to the user to copy, and upstream's
# test_subagent asserts it is in the tree. Un-ignore that one file.
!agent/subagent/assets/README.md

# Local brainstorm / visual companion sessions
.superpowers/

